COLOURFASTNESS TEST REPORTS
Test reports for the Blush polyester blouse, colourfastness to rubbing (ISO 105-X12)
Product: Blush Blouse, STY-4012 (SKU-100007, SKU-100014, SKU-100021), pink polyester, fabric MAT-POL-100
Test period: reports issued across the last two months, one report per bulk lot
Pass requirement: rubbing grade 4 or better, dry and wet (grey scale 1-5)

TEST RESULTS (7 bulk lots, all failed):
Report 1: BATCH-POL-PINK-001, dye lot DYE-900001, colour Pink. Dry 2, wet 2. FAIL - red-pink transfer onto white test cloth
Report 2: BATCH-POL-PINK-002, dye lot DYE-900002, colour Pink. Dry 2, wet 2. FAIL - heavy colour transfer
Report 3: BATCH-POL-PINK-003, dye lot DYE-900003, colour Pink. Dry 3, wet 2. FAIL - moderate transfer
Report 4: BATCH-POL-PINK-004, dye lot DYE-900004, colour Pink. Dry 2, wet 2. FAIL - heavy colour transfer
Report 5: BATCH-POL-PINK-005, dye lot DYE-900005, colour Pink. Dry 2, wet 2. FAIL - heavy colour transfer
Report 6: BATCH-POL-PINK-006, dye lot DYE-900006, colour Pink. Dry 3, wet 3. FAIL - moderate transfer
Report 7: BATCH-POL-PINK-007, dye lot DYE-900007, colour Pink. Dry 2, wet 2. FAIL - heavy colour transfer

OBSERVATIONS FROM THE TEST LAB:
- All seven lots are the same pink shade; no other colour of this blouse was reported failing in the period.
- Worst results (grade 2) are on lots 001, 002, 004, 005 and 007.
- The reports do not record the dye house, mill or process changes; cross-check those against the dye lot records.
- Fabric fibre content and weave are identical on all seven lots (100% polyester).
